 "scope": "Curve25519 one-pass affine consequence compiler, fixed native controls v1",
 "statement": "Unsigned pure-Rust fixed controls:34 sealed quadratic requests yield checked original-linear-row lineage and quadratic telescoping certificates while retaining every original variable/equation. All28 matched curve inputs have unchanged before/after node counts and outcome classes under the same v1 Worklist limits:13 original toy Unsupported,13 indexed toy roots,2 actual q1/two-column roots, each repeated before/after with original independent equation and indexed/group replay. Thus no observed branching gain for this fixed one-pass variant. Large original1059/1089 and indexed1989/2223 inputs append to1174/2548 equations with37/157 pivots, maxdegree2 and ZERO solver calls. Four small Fp29 truth domains and canonical certificate/request corruption/cap controls retained; coupled linear fixture changes Unsupported to checked Root. All64 source inputs/four source archive roundtrips/nine compiled pins and immutable binary/qualifier match. Historical standalone Python-launched interface receipts excluded from acceptance pending thin-shell replacement. No complete-cost, timing, live-memory, huge-base solve, signed/formal verification, generic solving-degree bound or exponent claim."
